# Poly(para-phenylene). The flat bands (antisymmetric under the mirror along the chain)
# cross the frontier bands, so the bands are picked by their weight on the sites (auto).
# The mirror-symmetric sector is an exact 4-site chain  P1 - Q1 - Q2 - P2 - P1' ...
#   P  = para carbon,  Q = symmetric combination of the two ortho carbons
bands auto
site P1 near 0.71 0
site Q1 near 1.42 1.23   1.42 -1.23
site Q2 near 2.84 1.23   2.84 -1.23
site P2 near 3.55 0
onsite P1 eP
onsite P2 eP
onsite Q1 eQ
onsite Q2 eQ
hop P1 Q1 0 tPQ          # through the ring (sqrt(2) t for nearest neighbours)
hop Q2 P2 0 tPQ
hop Q1 Q2 0 tQQ          # ring bond parallel to the chain
hop P2 P1 1 tinter       # inter-ring bond
# longer-range terms, needed with 2nd/3rd-neighbour hopping (they fit to 0 for NN only)
hop P1 Q2 0 tPQ2         # para - meta
hop Q1 P2 0 tPQ2
hop Q2 P1 1 tPQ2
hop P2 Q1 1 tPQ2
hop P1 P2 0 tPP          # para - para across the ring
hop Q2 Q1 1 tQQ2         # across the inter-ring bond
